# Checker profiles used by the demo image

Start with [Try Haskoki](../../../docs/try-it.md) for runnable Docker commands.
These files configure `haskoki-demo check` and `compare`; the entrypoint
sources `profiles.conf` and copies `backend-memory.toml` into each run.

## Profiles

| Profile | Selection | Current result, direct and proxied |
| --- | --- | --- |
| smoke | Offline interface, slot, digest, and profile cases | 743 collected cases; zero findings; exit 0 |
| full | All offline cases | 10983 collected cases; 18 documented findings in each mode (v0.5 re-freeze); exit 1 |

Collected cases include skips and expected failures. They are not counts
of passing tests. The checker is pinned to 0.2.3 and the proxy to v0.2.2.
`scripts/test-demo-image.sh` checks the exact finding sets; current counters
and measured counters are in [demo results](../../../docs/release-results.md).

The selections exclude vector corpora, stress, fuzz, and slow cases.
Large vector collections are optional downloads, as described in that
results page. The per-test timeout is 180 seconds direct and 360 proxied.

## Backend and reports

The backend uses an in-memory store and real OpenSSL crypto. The checker
creates its own keys; demo PINs 1234/5678 are public fixtures. Direct runs
use `HASKOKI_CONFIG`; proxy runs give the configuration to the daemon.

To keep reports, mount a writable host directory at `/out`, as shown in
the hands-on guide. Each run produces `results.json` (checker counters),
`report.jsonl` (per-case outcomes), `report.json` (demo command result),
and `findings.txt`. The comparison's frozen exclusions and reasons are in
the adjacent `compare-classify/frozen-subset.tsv`; they are not provisional.
